 ## Project Structure & Module Organization
 
-agenteam is an AI Agent collaboration platform with design documents, a Go foundation, PostgreSQL/pgvector migrations and transactions, Central/unconnected Runner processes, and a runnable Vue frontend with shared components and a development-only Debug page. Central requires its database, independent cursor/Secret/download/account keyrings, a restricted account recovery log, security initialization, DB outbound policy, verified MinIO runtime and the transactional Outbox before serving diagnostics and account HTTP. Account/Session, invitations, password recovery, profile/avatar/preferences and account System administration are bound to real services. SMTP delivery and restricted-log recovery use the sole production Outbox handler `account.mail-enqueue`; System authorization and exact-user avatar object authorization are bound. Typed Audit, signed cursors, encrypted Secret storage/leases, controlled outbound access, object/Artifact/download libraries and typed Runner transfer storage are implemented. Project, execution/binding, Artifact/download HTTP, Runner transfer authorization/protocol and Provider/MCP consumers remain unbound in the production root. `/readyz` remains 503; D26/D27 product UI and other future bindings are not complete.
+agenteam is an AI Agent collaboration platform with design documents, a Go foundation, PostgreSQL/pgvector migrations and transactions, Central/unconnected Runner processes, and a runnable Vue frontend with shared components and a development-only Debug page. Central requires its database, independent cursor/Secret/download/account keyrings, a restricted account recovery log, security initialization, DB outbound policy, verified MinIO runtime and the transactional Outbox before serving diagnostics, account HTTP and System Model configuration HTTP. Account/Session, invitations, password recovery, profile/avatar/preferences and account System administration are bound to real services. System Provider/Model CRUD, the platform selector, Model credentials and both command lookup routes use real Account Session/admin authorization, Secret, typed Audit and the same event journal. Secret initialization precedes Model initialization under the same startup context/deadline. SMTP delivery and restricted-log recovery use the sole production Outbox handler `account.mail-enqueue`; Model events persist without Model subscriptions or consumers. System authorization and exact-user avatar object authorization are bound. Typed Audit, signed cursors, encrypted Secret storage/leases, controlled outbound access, object/Artifact/download libraries and typed Runner transfer storage are implemented.
+
+Project, execution/binding, Artifact/download HTTP, Runner transfer authorization/protocol, Model Resolver/Invocation/Usage and actual Provider/MCP calls remain unbound in the production root. Summary defaults remain undecided, and complete D09 is not delivered. The [known Object runtime join defect](docs/development/agent-team/object-runtime-join-regression.md) remains unresolved; the System Model root result does not repair it. `/readyz` remains 503 and `ready=false`; D26/D27 product UI and other future bindings are not complete.
 
 - `cmd/agenteam/` and `cmd/agenteam-runner/`: Central and Runner entry points.
 - `internal/central/` and `internal/runner/`: respective implementations; `internal/runnerprotocol/`: shared communication contracts. Runner must not import Central business packages.
